{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Fair Trading Board - Aerie Exchange{% endblock %}

{% block meta %}
	<meta name="description" content="The District's Fair Trading Board: who heads it and the screens a merger must clear.">
	<meta property="og:title" content="Fair Trading Board | Aerie Exchange">
	<meta property="og:type" content="website">
{% endblock %}

{% macro hhi(value) %}<span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ value|hhi }}</span>{% endmacro %}

{% block body %}
{% import _self as fmt %}
<div class="max-w-400 mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pt-8 pb-12 w-full space-y-6">

	{% include 'government/_breadcrumb.html.twig' with {current: 'Fair Trading Board'} %}
	<header class="pb-5 border-b border-outline-variant/15">
		<h1 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold text-on-surface tracking-tight">Fair Trading Board</h1>
		<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
			Reviews the mergers of the District's firms. Its head is named by the Aerie Council for a single term and sets
			the guidelines a deal must clear: how concentrated a market may become, and how much of it one firm may hold.
		</p>
	</header>

	{% if board %}
		{% set head = board.head %}
		{% set screens = board.screens %}
		<section class="bg-surface-container-low rounded-lg p-5 border border-outline-variant/20" aria-labelledby="head-heading">
			<h2 id="head-heading" class="text-sm font-semibold text-on-surface">The head</h2>
			<p class="text-sm font-semibold text-on-surface mt-2">{{ head.name }}</p>
			<p class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant mt-0.5">Age {{ head.age }} · seated {{ head.sinceLabel }} · term ends <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ head.termEndsLabel }}</span></p>
			<p class="text-sm text-on-surface mt-2 max-w-3xl">
				{{- {light: 'Would let firms consolidate', balanced: 'Takes a middle course', strict: 'A strict enforcer against concentration'}[head.stance] }},
				{{ head.opening ? 'keeping the guidelines the District had at Year 1' : 'drawing the concentration line at' }}
				{%- if not head.opening %} {{ fmt.hhi(screens.concentrated) }} on the HHI{% endif %}
				{%- if head.passedOver is not empty %}, chosen over {% for candidate in head.passedOver %}{{ candidate.name }} <span class="text-on-surface-variant">({{ fmt.hhi(candidate.line) }}, {{ candidate.age }})</span>{{ loop.last ? '' : (loop.revindex == 2 ? ' and ' : ', ') }}{% endfor %}{% endif %}.
			</p>
			<p class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant mt-2 max-w-3xl">
				The Council names the head for a single {{ board.rules.termYears|number_format(0) }}-year term from a shortlist of {{ board.rules.shortlist }}, choosing the candidate nearest its own view of competition.
				{% if board.councilLine is not null %}The Council's median member would draw the line at {{ fmt.hhi(board.councilLine) }}.{% endif %}
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="bg-surface-container-low rounded-lg p-5 border border-outline-variant/20" aria-labelledby="screens-heading">
			<h2 id="screens-heading" class="text-sm font-semibold text-on-surface">The guidelines in force</h2>
			<dl class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-x-6 gap-y-4 mt-3">
				<div>
					<dt class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant">Concentration line</dt>
					<dd class="mt-1 text-2xl font-semibold text-on-surface">{{ fmt.hhi(screens.concentrated) }}</dd>
					<dd class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant">HHI, the sum of the squared market shares</dd>
				</div>
				<div>
					<dt class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant">Safe harbour</dt>
					<dd class="mt-1 text-2xl font-semibold text-on-surface">{{ fmt.hhi(screens.delta) }}</dd>
					<dd class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant">HHI points a deal may add whatever the market</dd>
				</div>
				<div>
					<dt class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant">Largest merged firm</dt>
					<dd class="mt-1 text-2xl font-semibold text-on-surface">{% if screens.shareCeiling < 1 %}<span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ screens.shareCeiling|pct(0) }}</span>{% else %}No cap{% endif %}</dd>
					<dd class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant">of its market</dd>
				</div>
			</dl>
			<p class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant mt-4 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
				A deal is presumed to lessen competition when it adds more than the safe harbour and either leaves its market above the concentration line or makes a firm larger than the cap.
				An acquirer buys only as much of its market as clears, so the guidelines decide how large a deal can be, and a deal too small to be worth doing once trimmed is dropped.
			</p>
			<p class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant mt-3 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
				A head may set the guidelines anywhere from the lightest on record, a line at {{ fmt.hhi(board.rules.lightest.concentrated) }} with a safe harbour of {{ fmt.hhi(board.rules.lightest.delta) }} and no cap on share,
				to the strictest, a line at {{ fmt.hhi(board.rules.strictest.concentrated) }}, a safe harbour of {{ fmt.hhi(board.rules.strictest.delta) }} and a cap of <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ board.rules.strictest.shareCeiling|pct(0) }}</span>.
				Each listed company's page shows where its own market stands against them.
			</p>
		</section>
	{% else %}
		<p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant">The Fair Trading Board has no head yet.</p>
	{% endif %}

	<p class="source-note">{{ source_line('fair-trading-board') }}</p>
</div>
{% endblock %}
